# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and turns it into response headers.
# It is a plain-text file at the root of what gets uploaded — if the deploy is
# a drag-and-drop of the site files, THIS FILE HAS TO BE IN THE DRAG. There is
# no error if it is missing; the headers simply do not appear, and nothing on
# the site looks any different. Check for it after a deploy.
#
# Why a CSP at all: the whole CMS rests on "owner-typed text goes onto the page
# as text, never as markup" — createElement and textContent, never innerHTML.
# That rule is enforced by discipline and by tools/test-copy.mjs. This file is
# the second line: if the rule is ever broken, a CSP turns a stored-XSS breach
# into a blocked request in the console.
#
# It is strict because it can be. The site has no inline scripts, no inline
# style attributes and no third-party origins — the fonts were the last one and
# they are self-hosted now. Verified by tools/check-csp.mjs, which fails the
# build if anything is added that this policy would silently block.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://yofoiqgknsqzsuwtlqvh.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://yofoiqgknsqzsuwtlqvh.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()

# Notes on the individual directives, because the next person to change one
# will want to know what it is holding up:
#
#   script-src 'self'      No 'unsafe-inline'. The JSON-LD blocks are
#                          type="application/ld+json", which browsers never
#                          execute and CSP therefore does not gate — render.js
#                          fills them with textContent, which is DOM work and
#                          not script evaluation. Adding one inline <script>
#                          anywhere breaks the whole site under this policy.
#
#   style-src 'self'       No 'unsafe-inline', which is only safe because
#                          there are zero style="…" attributes in the markup.
#                          script.js sets custom properties through
#                          el.style.setProperty — that is CSSOM and is not
#                          gated. A style attribute added to any page would be
#                          silently dropped, which is exactly the kind of
#                          breakage that gets blamed on CSS.
#
#   font-src 'self' data:  The two critical faces are inlined in styles.css as
#                          data: URIs. Without data: here the site loads in
#                          Georgia and the nav shifts on every navigation —
#                          see the section at the top of memory.md.
#
#   img-src                'self' for the photographs the site ships with,
#                          data: for the couple of inline SVGs, and the one
#                          Supabase project for photographs the owner has
#                          uploaded. The storage origin is the same host as
#                          connect-src and has to stay in step with config.js;
#                          without it every replaced photograph is a broken
#                          image and the console is the only place that says
#                          why. Checked by tools/check-csp.mjs.
#
#   connect-src            'self' plus exactly one Supabase project. data.js
#                          talks to /rest/v1/ there and nowhere else. If the
#                          project ref in config.js ever changes, it has to
#                          change here too or the site silently stops seeing
#                          live content and falls back to the seeds — which
#                          looks like everything working.
#
#   frame-ancestors 'self' Nobody *else* may put this site in an iframe. It was
#                          'none' until Phase 5, and the change is deliberate:
#                          the editor checks a headline's length by loading the
#                          real page into a hidden frame, putting the candidate
#                          text into the real element and counting the line
#                          boxes. That is the only way to measure the wrap
#                          without duplicating the site's type — and duplicated
#                          type is type that drifts.
#
#                          'self' gives up nothing that mattered. Clickjacking
#                          is an attack by a page on *another* origin, which
#                          'self' still refuses; a same-origin frame can already
#                          read and script the page it framed. The admin page
#                          below keeps 'none' — it is the one holding a session
#                          token, and nothing needs to frame it.

# The editor page. It holds the owner's session token in localStorage, so an
# injected script there is worth more to an attacker than one on a menu page.
# Same policy, minus data: everywhere it is not needed, and no framing at all.
/admin.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://yofoiqgknsqzsuwtlqvh.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://yofoiqgknsqzsuwtlqvh.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# img-src on the admin page also allows blob: and the Supabase origin, because
# Phase 6 previews an upload from a blob URL before it exists on the server and
# shows the stored photo afterwards. Stated here rather than added in a hurry
# later, when the symptom will be a blank thumbnail and no obvious cause.
